00:27:57,233 --> 00:27:58,890
It's not a mind game.

453
00:27:58,970 --> 00:28:03,680
They don't play chess. Because all the mind games are forbidden. So no one plays chess.

454
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:07,680
Ludo is like pure luck, any number comes, snake comes, ladder comes.

455
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:11,680
Anyway, it is extremely unfortunate.

456
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:16,680
One thing we have is that the spaces, the youth-centric spaces, should be there.

457
00:28:16,760 --> 00:28:17,680
They are not like that.

458
00:28:17,760 --> 00:28:20,680
Karachi used to have a lot of parks, a lot of grounds.

459
00:28:20,760 --> 00:28:26,680
But some grounds were taken by political parties that they became related to them.

460
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:29,760
Now, in Nishtar Park, I don't think anyone goes to play cricket.

461
00:28:30,100 --> 00:28:32,459
There were only water parties.

462
00:28:32,539 --> 00:28:37,500
Similarly, many community parks were taken over and apartments were built.

463
00:28:37,580 --> 00:28:44,220
I mean, there are so many parks. In my college, there used to be something or the other in every lane.

464
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:47,843
But recently, I went there and I was shooting something.

465
00:28:47,923 --> 00:28:51,740
There is a high rise of 8 floors because the population is so high.

466
00:28:51,820 --> 00:28:57,130
It's a lucrative industry, real estate. So they take over and then you give bribe and build a building.

467
00:28:57,210 --> 00:29:03,930
In Gulshan-e-Iqbal, there's a road from Karachi to Abul Hasan Isfahani Road.

468
00:29:04,010 --> 00:29:07,350
If you're coming towards Disco Bakery, there's a building in the middle.

469
00:29:07,430 --> 00:29:11,150
There's a road on both sides and a building in the middle.

470
00:29:11,230 --> 00:29:13,490
And he divided the road into two parts.

471
00:29:13,570 --> 00:29:20,370
Can you imagine that in a city like Karachi, someone built a whole complex on 20 streets?

472
00:29:20,450 --> 00:29:23,370
And nobody questioned that person. How many people will be involved?

473
00:29:23,450 --> 00:29:24,950
So where these circumstances are…

474
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:27,580
There are no outdoor activities left.

475
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:33,580
And I always say that it's very important, especially for youth, because they're full of energy.

476
00:29:33,660 --> 00:29:36,580
So their energy should be invested in something productive.

477
00:29:36,660 --> 00:29:43,580
When I went to Vienna, this was pre-COVID or after COVID? I don't remember. I think, yes, pre-COVID.

478
00:29:43,660 --> 00:29:47,580
Yeah, my son wasn't in the world, so yeah, pre-COVID.

479
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:53,600
So I went to a place where there was a whole space and that was a…

480
00:29:53,900 --> 00:29:56,820
He was a skateboarder and he had an NGO named after him.

481
00:29:56,900 --> 00:30:00,486
He made it for youth because there was a point where,

482
00:30:00,566 --> 00:30:05,820
I think maybe in the 1980s or the 1990s, Vienna had a very huge drug problem.

483
00:30:05,900 --> 00:30:07,820
Like class A drugs.

484
00:30:07,900 --> 00:30:15,820
So he figured out that maybe his friend had died or something and then he figured out he understood the need to channelize energy.

485
00:30:15,900 --> 00:30:19,820
So he has a whole skateboard park because he was a skateboarder himself.

486
00:30:19,900 --> 00:30:21,780
And then there was a wall, that daily wall.

487
00:30:21,860 --> 00:30:25,980
The walls change and get painted and kids come and just graffiti.

488
00:30:26,060 --> 00:30:30,500
You get free paints there. Kids come and graffiti, some do rollerblade.

489
00:30:30,580 --> 00:30:37,620
And then there was another room where there was very loud heavy metal music playing and then kids were like just listening to that and they were shaking.

490
00:30:37,700 --> 00:30:42,500
They were just channelizing their anger.

491
00:30:42,580 --> 00:30:47,980
Similarly, I saw the same thing in Melbourne CBD. There were also such spaces there. Kids were graffitiing.

492
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:52,839
You see the streets are filled with graffiti.

493
00:30:52,919 --> 00:30:56,900
Similarly, I think wherever I've been, I've seen youth-centric spaces.

494
00:30:56,980 --> 00:31:02,900
I've told you about Karachi, where everyone was eaten. Then when nothing was left, then mobile phones were also used.

495
00:31:02,980 --> 00:31:09,900
Right around the time when China cut off people's land, apartments were built on the ground of the cemetery. So what can you do?

496
00:31:09,980 --> 00:31:13,900
At the same time, cable came and then mobile phones came, so children were left here.

497
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:16,470
Then outdoor spaces are not safe either.

498
00:31:16,550 --> 00:31:18,204
This is also a big problem.

499
00:31:18,284 --> 00:31:22,708
But among all odds, if you want more than the problem, for example,

500
00:31:22,788 --> 00:31:27,358
if I want to read a book and I know that it is available in the library,

501
00:31:27,438 --> 00:31:30,561
but I also know that there are problems in between,

502
00:31:30,641 --> 00:31:34,785
so I'll find a way to get there and read that book.

503
00:31:34,865 --> 00:31:36,739
But we have no more desire.

504
00:31:36,819 --> 00:31:40,084
Again, children then see what the elders are seeing.

505
00:31:40,164 --> 00:31:41,756
Now what do our elders do?

506
00:31:41,836 --> 00:31:43,740
I have said this in so many videos.

507
00:31:43,820 --> 00:31:52,540
They are born to be married and have a purpose in life.

508
00:31:52,620 --> 00:31:57,000
They don't raise their children like that.

509
00:31:57,080 --> 00:32:00,880
Children look at their parents and say that their mothers don't do anything and their fathers don't do anything either.

510
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,620
They don't have any other hobby.

511
00:32:02,700 --> 00:32:06,660
They don't read books or have any conversation.

512
00:32:06,740 --> 00:32:08,700
They start with politics and end with politics.

513
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:10,540
There was a time when…

514
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:16,900
There was only one TV in the house, so between 8 and 10 women used to have a remote because dramas would come on.

515
00:32:16,980 --> 00:32:19,380
After 10, maybe Masood and then all this used to happen.

516
00:32:19,460 --> 00:32:21,380
So they switched to Abu.

517
00:32:21,460 --> 00:32:26,940
Now there is a TV in every room or there is a TV in the hand, so politics is going on or dramas are going on.

518
00:32:27,020 --> 00:32:28,940
Both are non-productive things.

519
00:32:29,020 --> 00:32:33,660
Then the youth, if we talk about Pakistan, then it has been put in politics.

520
00:32:33,740 --> 00:32:38,420
Again, I am not saying that youth should be apolitical, but youth should not be a cult either.

521
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:40,720
We need to balance things.

522
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:43,800
Now they don't do anything.

523
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:50,975
I read a very good post that if you don't read books or travel or don't learn new things,

524
00:32:51,055 --> 00:32:54,720
then you have nothing left but to show your wealth.

525
00:32:54,800 --> 00:33:00,107
So you see in Pakistan, people with all the means in the world,

526
00:33:00,187 --> 00:33:06,800
they show their BMW logo or Gucci bag because they have nothing to talk about.

527
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:12,276
When you read, when you ponder, when you think about things,

528
00:33:12,356 --> 00:33:18,944
what's happening in the world, you talk to an average kid, unfortunately,

529
00:33:19,024 --> 00:33:22,000
he is not so aware of the world.

530
00:33:22,080 --> 00:33:25,400
What's going on in the world? His approach is very straight forward, very linear approach.

531
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:27,030
That brother, now I am born.

532
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:32,544
If I want to come to a conservative house or my liberal house or a centrist house,

533
00:33:32,624 --> 00:33:34,080
then this is my approach.

534
00:33:34,170 --> 00:33:37,370
I have to get married, get a job, go abroad, have children and die.

535
00:33:37,450 --> 00:33:39,610
There is no meaning in life.

536
00:33:39,690 --> 00:33:43,650
How does that meaning come? That meaning comes only when you sit idle.

537
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:46,650
When you have nothing to do and you think about it.

538
00:33:46,730 --> 00:33:48,130
We have stopped thinking.

539
00:33:48,210 --> 00:33:54,050
And then it remains that take the car to Margalla Hill, it will become a good snap.

540
00:33:54,130 --> 00:33:58,410
Or then in Karachi, at night, all the cars are making a snap.

541
00:33:58,490 --> 00:34:00,490
Because they have nothing else to do.

542
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:05,280
There's no meaningful conversation, no events like this.

543
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:10,220
The literary events are boring.

544
00:34:10,300 --> 00:34:13,660
There's no tea, nothing at home.

545
00:34:13,740 --> 00:34:15,820
So, there's nothing left but a hobby.

546
00:34:15,900 --> 00:34:20,660
People used to write in their resumes, what was your hobby? Internet surfing.

547
00:34:20,740 --> 00:34:24,180
What kind of hobby is this? What do you do on the internet? Do you read something?

548
00:34:24,260 --> 00:34:27,260
Do you play anything?

549
00:34:27,360 --> 00:34:32,840
I got a job in Dubai. A lot of people came to the job and asked me, what are your hobbies?

550
00:34:32,920 --> 00:34:39,160
So I said, on this side I'm a stand-up comedian. And he said, leave it, tell me a joke. I told him a joke and I got hired.

551
00:34:39,240 --> 00:34:42,773
These hobbies, these conversations are also a starter.

552
00:34:42,853 --> 00:34:47,858
One of my friends who is a bartender, he is an Indian guy, he will say a lot,

553
00:34:47,938 --> 00:34:50,240
I don't know who is doing a bad job.

554
00:34:50,320 --> 00:34:54,560
So he got a job on this.

555
00:34:54,870 --> 00:35:00,790
He was fit for the job, but I asked him what his hobby was. He said, I like to bartend. I said, okay, you'll make cocktails on Friday.

556
00:35:00,870 --> 00:35:05,790
So, conversation is an icebreaker. You have something to talk to, something meaningful.

557
00:35:05,870 --> 00:35:11,342
Or if you have a hobby of pets, or if you're an animal rescuer, if you look for animals,

558
00:35:11,422 --> 00:35:15,790
you get satisfaction in your personal life, you get meaning in your life.

559
00:35:15,870 --> 00:35:22,250
Plus, if you're going on Bumble or Tinder, then that's something to talk about. And then obviously, you know.

560
00:35:22,330 --> 00:35:25,250
women find it attractive or men find it attractive.

561
00:35:25,330 --> 00:35:28,250
This is what she likes to do and this is what he likes to do.

562
00:35:28,330 --> 00:35:34,290
So this adds value to your personality in every way, whether it's professional life,

563
00:35:34,370 --> 00:35:37,250
corporate life, personal life, whatever.

564
00:35:37,330 --> 00:35:39,250
So this is very important.

565
00:35:39,330 --> 00:35:43,250
So it's very important, whether it's your book reading or whatever.

566
00:35:43,330 --> 00:35:46,250
One more thing, you mentioned about DIY, the DIY community.

567
00:35:46,330 --> 00:35:48,150
Now I noticed something very important.

568
00:35:48,230 --> 00:35:53,710
I notice that we have to call a mechanic for every small thing.

569
00:35:53,790 --> 00:35:56,710
We have to call a carpenter or an electrician for every small thing.

570
00:35:56,790 --> 00:35:59,620
We don't know how to do this, nor are we taught in schools.

571
00:35:59,700 --> 00:36:04,064
There should be a class that you have to connect small circuits like this,

572
00:36:04,144 --> 00:36:08,575
or you have to tune your car like this, or you have to change the oil like this,

573
00:36:08,655 --> 00:36:12,190
or you have to put the puncture like this, or anything like that.

574
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:16,260
There is no such arrangement. I think it should be a community thing.

575
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:18,940
Our housing societies have become so big.

576
00:36:19,020 --> 00:36:22,020
So do something meaningful for the children there.

577
00:36:22,100 --> 00:36:26,740
Just say that there is a hospital, a school and all the facilities are there.

578
00:36:26,820 --> 00:36:31,820
So this is also an facility where people see that parents are very sentimental about their kids.

579
00:36:31,900 --> 00:36:36,140
Where they will feel that our children will get to play and jump outdoors.

580
00:36:36,220 --> 00:36:37,980
He will also get something to learn.

581
00:36:38,060 --> 00:36:42,940
How difficult it is. You keep a DIY class in the community and WhatsApp Messenger.

582
00:36:43,140 --> 00:36:51,020
Leave a message on Facebook group that this is a DIY class, free for all.

583
00:36:51,100 --> 00:36:53,700
Or you can invest 500 rupees per head.

584
00:36:53,780 --> 00:37:00,020
There is a community living here in Emaar, so we will teach kids how to do it.

585
00:37:00,100 --> 00:37:07,020
What is the need to take out the car and go all the way to Gizri and then say, you are a carpenter, you come, you do this, you put cement, you paint.

586
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:09,900
Making cement should come by itself, painting should come by itself.

587
00:37:11,070 --> 00:37:15,190
In movies and English movies, girls paint themselves at home.

588
00:37:15,270 --> 00:37:17,190
They are wearing bandanas.

589
00:37:17,270 --> 00:37:19,190
This work should come on its own.

590
00:37:19,270 --> 00:37:24,390
Again, we are officers.

591
00:37:24,470 --> 00:37:27,390
The whole country is a royal country.

592
00:37:27,470 --> 00:37:29,390
I will throw money and get work done.

593
00:37:29,470 --> 00:37:31,190
I have nothing to learn.

594
00:37:31,270 --> 00:37:33,190
Nor do I have any desires.

595
00:37:33,270 --> 00:37:37,190
So again, in such societies, hobbies are left to be done.

596
00:37:37,270 --> 00:37:39,050
I like shopping.

597
00:37:39,130 --> 00:37:42,410
I like listening to music, or this and that.

598
00:37:42,490 --> 00:37:46,410
We don't go to the music instrument side either because it's haram.

599
00:37:46,490 --> 00:37:47,770
We don't learn chess either.

600
00:37:47,850 --> 00:37:53,450
I mean, where there's a brain, a skill, a move of a person's hands and feet, we don't go.

601
00:37:53,530 --> 00:37:58,131
I was really glad to see when I was doing a Q&A and someone asked me,

602
00:37:58,211 --> 00:38:00,570
what's your favorite Metallica song?

603
00:38:00,650 --> 00:38:01,930
And I said, Fade to Black.

604
00:38:02,010 --> 00:38:05,690
So a fifteen year old kid who lives in Bariyaton, born and bred in Saudi.

605
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:10,360
He played the guitar so well. And then he said, this is broken, I'm saving it for a new one.

606
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:12,360
I feel like I should get him a new guitar.

607
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:16,360
He played so well. I'm so happy to meet kids like this.

608
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:22,560
That he's sitting at home playing Fade to Black or Guns N' Roses. It's really nice.

609
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:27,360
So this comes from the parents and the parents should enforce it.

610
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:30,760
What do parents do? The kid is crying, they give the iPad, the kid is crying, they give the iPhone.

611
00:38:30,840 --> 00:38:33,330
Yesterday I was watching a reel.

612
00:38:33,410 --> 00:38:39,490
It was a real Indian mother, a single mother, and I saved money and got my son a mobile phone.

613
00:38:39,570 --> 00:38:44,530
And you're getting your son a flip phone for 2,500,000. What's the point of that?

614
00:38:44,610 --> 00:38:47,490
He's going to school, he's in uniform, and he's buying it.

615
00:38:47,570 --> 00:38:53,490
So parents, they need to also invest.

616
00:38:53,570 --> 00:38:58,570
Now, obviously, my baby is a COVID baby, so the screen time is more.

617
00:38:58,650 --> 00:39:00,580
So I bought Hot Wheels.

618
00:39:00,660 --> 00:39:06,580
I keep ordering it for him. Then I planned to get him, because we have, God willing, space big enough.

619
00:39:06,660 --> 00:39:13,580
So the whole track of the Hot Wheel, I want like, the whole house can't have a track, the cat has to break it.

620
00:39:13,660 --> 00:39:17,312
But it's good that he sits and builds, and then he has curiosity inside him,

621
00:39:17,392 --> 00:39:20,949
it's good that I built this thing, why is this car going faster from here,

622
00:39:21,029 --> 00:39:22,580
why is it accelerating like this.

623
00:39:22,660 --> 00:39:26,660
In that, curiosity will build and then he will find his own way.

624
00:39:27,450 --> 00:39:31,170
The rest of the kids pick up the things themselves.

625
00:39:31,250 --> 00:39:33,940
But again, if you have this much thought, this much vision,

626
00:39:34,020 --> 00:39:37,041
I have three sons.

627
00:39:37,121 --> 00:39:37,421
or this much vision for your children, then what is this?

628
00:39:37,501 --> 00:39:41,240
I will not mention their names, they are very good friends.

629
00:39:41,320 --> 00:39:44,989
Again, the purpose of having children is not excellence,

630
00:39:45,069 --> 00:39:47,555
not the excellence of their lives, but to show people that,

631
00:39:47,635 --> 00:39:54,830
It is written in front of their house.

632
00:39:55,420 --> 00:39:58,180
Three? Three arm house?

633
00:39:58,840 --> 00:39:59,840
I was like, what is this?

634
00:40:00,140 --> 00:40:01,140
He has three sons.

635
00:40:01,740 --> 00:40:04,660
So, three arms of a father. Not three, but six.

636
00:40:04,740 --> 00:40:06,940
Arms must be six.

637
00:40:07,020 --> 00:40:09,800
I mean, this is the breadth that uncle has three sons.

638
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:12,200
Did you make it yourself?

639
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:15,040
If you made it yourself, then you must have had a few shocks.

640
00:40:15,120 --> 00:40:19,000
If you made it with your hands, then this is a pride level checker.

641
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:21,200
I have three sons. What is this?

642
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,370
What do they do?

643
00:40:22,450 --> 00:40:25,370
What is their excellence? What is their success?

644
00:40:25,450 --> 00:40:28,370
What is the benefit for people because of them?

645
00:40:28,450 --> 00:40:31,370
It's a loss. Six cars are standing in the street.

646
00:40:31,450 --> 00:40:36,370
All houses, three arm houses, all these small streets, they surround all.

647
00:40:36,450 --> 00:40:39,370
So what is contribution? This matters.

648
00:40:39,450 --> 00:40:41,370
So yes, hobbies are very important.

649
00:40:41,450 --> 00:40:46,370
Not only does it add value to your life, it gives meaning, it nurtures you.

650
00:40:46,450 --> 00:40:49,270
And it gives you something to talk about.

651
00:40:49,350 --> 00:40:53,070
And then you know, someone wants to experiment with coffee.

652
00:40:53,150 --> 00:40:55,590
One of my friends has a passion for experimenting with coffee.

653
00:40:55,670 --> 00:40:58,870
He was putting in that itself that I should make this mix and do this and do that.

654
00:40:58,950 --> 00:41:02,390
So again, some hobbies are very expensive hobbies.

655
00:41:02,470 --> 00:41:03,910
I'm not saying that everyone should go that way.

656
00:41:03,990 --> 00:41:06,790
But like anything within your reach, you need to pursue.

657
00:41:06,870 --> 00:41:12,110
Your life will have a new color and then you'll have something to look forward to.

658
00:41:12,190 --> 00:41:16,360
Like that Goglu, my friend, he used to come to gaming magazines at some point.

659
00:41:16,440 --> 00:41:21,640
So he would go to get the car and then he would tell them to keep the car safe.

660
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:23,240
Don't sell it to anyone.

661
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:28,440
One of my friends used to read a lot of detective novels.

662
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:31,960
But this is like pre-internet era, so that time was different.

663
00:41:32,040 --> 00:41:36,280
So he would sit in the bus and go far away and then select the magazine.

664
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:38,360
It was like a fun thing to do.

665
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:43,880
I used to look for cassettes, audio cassettes, if I could find any good one.

666
00:41:44,940 --> 00:41:48,140
It's cheap. TDK's quality was very good.

667
00:41:48,220 --> 00:41:53,140
So yeah, have something in your life. It'll add more value. Take care. Thank you.

668
00:41:53,220 --> 00:41:57,140
Next question. To flee or not to flee when at gunpoint?

669
00:41:57,220 --> 00:42:01,140
Can you outrun a bullet? No. Next question. No, I'm just joking.

670
00:42:01,220 --> 00:42:07,940
Greetings, good sir. I never imagined that I would be one day writing an email to you, but this incident has made me compelled to do so.

671
00:42:08,020 --> 00:42:12,060
I know how much you hate haphazardly put emails, so I'll do my best to keep this.

672
00:42:12,140 --> 00:42:14,329
keep this one organized and easy to follow.

673
00:42:14,409 --> 00:42:16,435
Thank you for consideration.

674
00:42:16,515 --> 00:42:17,126
Furthermore,

